---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import {getBrandCharts} from "../lib/content/brand-charts";
const charts=getBrandCharts();
---
<BaseLayout title="Goalie Pad Sizing Calculator & Brand Charts | Goalie Gear Fit" description="Find your goalie leg-pad size using reviewed Bauer, CCM, TRUE, Warrior and Brian's charts, then verify the fit at the knee block." dateModified="2026-08-21">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="hero-photo" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/goalie-butterfly-hero.webp" alt="" width="1660" height="948" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"/></div>
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Independent goalie pad sizing</p><h1>Find your goalie pad size by brand.</h1><p class="hero-tagline">Land your knee. Not a guess.</p><p class="lede">Match your measurements against reviewed manufacturer rules, then take the result onto the ice for the only check that matters.</p><p class="hero-actions"><a class="button button--light" href="/calculator/">Find my pad size <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="text-link text-link--light" href="/guides/how-to-measure-goalie-pads/">How to measure <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p><p class="hero-proof"><span>5 brands reviewed</span><span>No nearest-size guesses</span><span>Sources shown</span></p></div>
    <div class="hero-caption"><span>Fit check</span><strong>Knee centered on the landing block</strong></div>
  </section>
  <section class="brand-section" aria-labelledby="brand-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed manufacturer data</p><h2 id="brand-heading">Start with the badge on your pad.</h2></div><p>Every brand uses its own chart logic. We keep those differences intact instead of forcing a false universal size.</p></div><div class="brand-grid">{charts.map(chart=><article class="brand-card"><img class:list={["brand-card__logo",{"brand-logo--inverse":chart.vendor.inverseLogo}]} src={chart.vendor.logoPath} alt="" width="140" height="48" loading="lazy"/><div><h3><a href={`/charts/${chart.slug}/`}>{chart.brand}</a></h3><p>{chart.rules.length} reviewed rules · {chart.categories.length} chart section{chart.categories.length===1?"":"s"}</p></div><span class="brand-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></article>)}</div><p class="section-action"><a href="/charts/">Compare all brand charts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></section>
  <section class="home-steps" aria-labelledby="steps-heading"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The fitting sequence</p><h2 id="steps-heading">From tape measure to crease.</h2></div><p>Three checks. In this order. The calculator narrows the field; your stance confirms the fit.</p></div><ol class="step-grid">
    <li><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M17 20h30a9 9 0 0 1 9 9v6a9 9 0 0 1-9 9H17a9 9 0 0 1-9-9v-6a9 9 0 0 1 9-9Z"/><path d="M18 20v10m8-10v6m8-6v10m8-10v6"/><circle cx="46" cy="34" r="4"/></svg></span><span class="step-number">01 · Measure</span><strong>Measure the right line.</strong><span>Floor-to-knee and ankle-to-knee are not interchangeable.</span></li>
    <li><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M13 10h38v44H13z"/><path d="M22 21h20M22 31h20M22 41h12"/><path class="accent" d="m39 43 4 4 9-11"/></svg></span><span class="step-number">02 · Match</span><strong>Match the actual chart.</strong><span>Overlaps show adjacent options. Missing evidence stays undetermined.</span></li>
    <li><span class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M8 12h19v40H8zM37 12h19v40H37z"/><path d="M13 18h9M42 18h9M13 46h9M42 46h9"/><path class="accent" d="M27 35h10"/></svg></span><span class="step-number">03 · Verify</span><strong>Drop into butterfly.</strong><span>With skates and protection on, confirm your knee lands securely on the block.</span></li>
  </ol></section>
  <section class="trust-section"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Why the answer may be “we can’t tell”</p><h2>Honest sizing stops where the chart stops.</h2></div><div><p>The charts come from reviewed manufacturer guidance, and each brand keeps the measurement method it actually publishes. We do not silently convert one method into another or fill missing evidence with a guessed size.</p><p>Use the chart result as a starting point, then verify knee-block landing and overall pad movement in your full setup.</p><p class="trust-links"><a href="/methodology/">Read our methodology</a><a href="/guides/thigh-rise-and-fit-check/">Run the fit check</a></p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
